_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:290:`cap_type_token` is only used to parse a *generic argument candidate*, not to admit a reserved capability as an ordinary value type. Operationally parse the common named argument prefix once, then classify by the declared kind; an ordinary `type` position rejects a capability-only name. This sharing avoids competing IDENT-started alternatives for types, brands and capability names. **OPEN-14** covers the exact kind-neutral argument AST/grammar, generic ordering and brand syntax; the notation above exposes the issue rather than pretending capabilities are value types.
