_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:398:The assertion production is a common-prefix parser proposal: parse the complete contract expression and record whether its root is a parenthesized group; only that grouped root admits optional `by path(args)`. An expression merely starting with `(`, such as `(a) == b`, has a binary root and does not qualify. This restriction reflects the approved `assert(e) by thm(...)` spelling; it is not an approved extension to `assert e by ...`.
