legacy/docs/spec/overview.md:65:| No hidden control flow | `a + b` on integers is primitive addition, not a call; the compiler never inserts a destructor call; allocation shows as `with(Alloc)`; a recoverable error leaves a function only through a written `return`. A `defer` is not hidden: the programmer writes it, its run point (the scope's exit) is visible from the block structure, and it calls exactly the function written. | OWN-12, OWN-13, TRUST-4, STMT-11 |
