legacy/docs/spec/memory.md:19:**MEM-D1@1.** At each program point a local binding is unconsumed, used (read or borrowed), consumed (moved), reserved (passed by value to a pending `defer`) or frozen (the owner of an enclosing borrow block, REF-D3), and reading or moving a Copy binding leaves its state unchanged, while a borrow block freezes it as any other.
legacy/docs/spec/memory.md:69:**Rationale.** Treating every address as concrete makes optimizations unsound, and treating every
legacy/docs/spec/memory.md:70:address as abstract makes integer-pointer round trips undefined. With quasi-concrete addresses,
legacy/docs/spec/memory.md:90:Indeterminate memory exists only behind trusted or `Unsafe` operations, as a named premise
legacy/docs/spec/memory.md:158:abort is the same as an arithmetic trap (ARITH-3). There is no global way to turn bounds checks
