legacy/docs/spec/ffi.md:272:**FFI-7@1.** The field order, offsets, padding, size and alignment of a struct or enum are unspecified except as a struct's `#[repr]` attribute fixes them (FFI-8), and safe code observes them only through `sizeof::<T>()` and `alignof::<T>()`, which give `T`'s size and alignment in bytes as a `u64`.
legacy/docs/spec/ffi.md:307:**FFI-8@2.** `#[repr(C)]` lays a struct out as C does, each field in declaration order at the next offset aligned for its type and the size rounded up to the struct's alignment, and `#[repr(packed)]` places the fields in declaration order with no padding and gives the struct alignment 1, accepts misaligned fields but refuses references to them (also when combined with `repr(C)`).
legacy/docs/spec/ffi.md:357:**FFI-9@1.** A `trusted extern fn` asserts, as an obligation of its author that the compiler does not check, that the foreign function is safe for every argument its parameter types permit and has no effect beyond those its `with(...)` declares.
