legacy/docs/spec/arithmetic.md:302:**ARITH-6@1.** An integer comparison is signed or unsigned as its operand type is, a float comparison follows IEEE 754 (every ordered comparison with a NaN operand is false, and `x == x` is false for a NaN), and a comparison reads its operands without moving them.
