legacy/docs/spec/references.md:61:**REF-D3@3.** A borrow block `borrow x as r { B }` freezes the local `x` for `B` and lends an ordinary `x: T` as `&T` (`borrow mut` as `&mut T`), but opens exactly one layer of `Heap<U, A>` (also through a shell reference) to its payload preserving the root and block lifetime and never upgrading shared access, while the exact heap-array view remains undecided (see [the target Core proposal](decisions.md#core-heap-array-view)), and the block ends its local loans and restores the owner state.
