legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:1958:**TYPE-D1@2.** A capability set is a set of capabilities (TRUST-D1) and capability variables, written as a comma-separated list in `with(...)` and as `{}` or names joined by `+` in a capability argument, and a function or a struct declares a capability variable as a parameter `<cap C>`.
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:1976:**TYPE-1@1.** A value of function type is a pointer to a named function, and any context the callee needs is passed to it as an explicit argument, so the language has no closures.
