legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:4204:#### ARITH-11. The named float conversions round as stated
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:4206:**ARITH-11@2.** A named conversion from an integer to a float, or from `f64` to `f32`, rounds to the nearest representable value with ties to even, and each float-to-integer rounding operation (`trunc`, `round`, `floor`, `ceil`) rounds as named and returns the resulting integer when representable, or an error as `try_convert` for NaN, infinities and results outside the target integer range.
