legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12410:  mutability and permitted positions, undecided on 2026-11-03, are provisionally decided by rows Q3.1–Q3.6 and Q4.7 ([rows](#decided-2026-11-05-core)); opening never yields an element reference.
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12450:The owner answered every row of the 2026-11-05 decision page, in the terminal. The rows that revise a recorded rule were answered one by one: Q5.1/Q5.4, Q6.4, Q2.8, Q9.15 with P3, Q7.11 and Q4.7. Q3.12, Q9.19, Q7.10, Q1.6, P2, P4, P9, P13, P16 and P17a/b were also answered directly. The remaining Core rows were accepted as recommended, and the remaining project rows were approved on the owner's condition that Claude and Codex agree and that each is the best long-term design (both confirmed; every row carries Codex agreement). The full rows (question, options, reason, recommendation, agreement, revision and notes) are in [core_rows.json](../archive/decisions-2026-11-05/core_rows.json) and [other_rows.json](../archive/decisions-2026-11-05/other_rows.json); the concrete rules behind them are in [R4_RATIONALE.md](../archive/decisions-2026-11-05/R4_RATIONALE.md), and where R4 and a row differ, the row governs.
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12458:- **TRAIT-1@1** (row Q2.8): two impls with equal heads may coexist only when Copy/Destroy disjointness (OD28) makes their domains disjoint, as in `impl<T: Copy> Destroy for Vec<T, A>` beside `impl<T: Destroy> Destroy for Vec<T, A>`. No other coherence or orphan rule changes, and no disjunctive bound syntax is added.
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12461:- **The text-only slice of R4 F4.3** (row Q4.7) is replaced before it was recorded: one scoped form opens every view, `borrow [mut] source [from a until b] as view { … } [else { … }]`. Without `else` an invalid range traps, like indexing; with `else` it is handled; a proven invalid range without `else` is refused (OD118). Arrays need `a ≤ b ≤ len`; text also needs UTF-8 scalar boundaries at both byte offsets.
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12462:- <a id="decided-2026-11-05-q6-2-fields"></a>**Q6.2 and R4 F12, known values through structs** (owner-approved revision, 2026-11-05, made during A2b): known values propagate field by field through immutable struct construction and destructuring. The checker tracks an abstract value for each binding: unknown, a known scalar, or a constructor whose fields carry their own abstract values. Constructing a struct records each field's fact independently; an immutable binding keeps the fact; destructuring hands each field's fact, recursively, to the corresponding immutable binder; an unknown component stays unknown without discarding its known siblings; an ownership transfer keeps the facts for the receiving binding without permitting reuse of the consumed one. Q6.2's exclusions stay (mutable state, branches and paths, user-function calls, calls outside the table, elaborator temporaries). So `let S { a } = S { a: 200u8 }; a + 100` is refused, in trusted and unreachable code too (OD118 as revised by Q6.4). Before this revision a field bound by destructuring was not known and that program was accepted and trapped.
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12507:- **Q4.6** What are dynamic string views? — Byte offsets; `byte_at` traps out of range; subviews only through the scoped borrow form of Q4.7 (`borrow t from a until b as s { … } [else { … }]`).
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12508:- **Q4.7** How are scoped views and range subviews introduced? — (a) borrow [mut] source [from a until b] as view { … } [else { … }]; no else = trap (like indexing); proven invalid range without else refused (OD118). *Revises or adds: Replaces R4 F4.3 text-only mandatory-else form; extends Q3.1/Q3.2 with subview formation; preserves OD36/OD118.*
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12514:- **Q6.2** Is local constant propagation mandatory? — Fixed table of statically known values: literals, immutable lets, module constants, checked ops, six named wrapping/saturating ops, lossless `as`. *Revised 2026-11-05: facts propagate field by field through immutable struct construction and destructuring ([revision](#decided-2026-11-05-q6-2-fields)).*
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12520:- **Q7.1** How are target grant schemas and multiplicities specified? — One target, linux-x86_64-hosted (Linux ≥ 5.6), with a fixed grant table; main asks for grants as parameters.
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12529:- **Q7.10** Do you approve the linux-x86_64-hosted grant table? — Approve R4 F6's complete grant table below as part of this row: every launch configuration, operation signature, permission, narrowing rule and ending contract. Standard-stream operations require Console (Q7.11), not Device; where the R4 F6 table says with(Device) for StdIn/StdOut/StdErr, read with(Console). A missing configured grant refuses startup with exit 125; a trap exits 134. *Revises or adds: New target contract: owner decision.*
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12534:- **Q8.4** Does the first artifact qualify as a complete executable? — Component plus bound launcher first.
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12542:- **Q9.5** Are heap opening and borrowing separate user mechanisms? — One surface borrow; distinct typed Core cases.
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12563:- **P4** Duplicate enum variants or methods (bug 313) — Refuse duplicate variant names in one enum and duplicate method names in one impl, with a new rule and diagnostic, the same as duplicate fields.
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12567:- **P8** Server services under scripts/ — Keep only landing services: train, review, hook, landing bot. The status page, work queue, fuzz farm, perf tracking and nightly campaign all stop and are recorded as archived in RETENTION.tsv; each returns only with a roadmap task.
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12570:- **P11** Std bugs and rulings are carried — Add a 'std' class: 12 std bugs move with std as contracts plus regressions. The 112 language rulings (26 still open) keep their ruling and become conformance examples.
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12572:- **P13** concrete-ci-2 as the only CI host — CI runs on concrete-ci-2 (self-hosted) and on GitHub-hosted runners as a regular second pool, not only a fallback. Jobs that need ci-2 caches run there; the oracle is fetched as a release asset verified by digest; a check neither pool can run is incomplete and blocks landing. Self-hosted runners never run pull_request jobs.
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12574:- **P15** New roadmap: retiring obligations — Accept the new single-file ROADMAP.md (wip/new-roadmap, reconciled: prepare → rehearse → move, assurance wording per Q8.1, Phase E per P18, decides nothing itself): 79 tasks kept as rows, 345 folded into area tasks with their obligations, 109 deferred with triggers, 7 retired, 15 done.
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12575:- **P16** Status changes in the refusal list — Accept the new statuses in PHILOSOPHY.md. Now Permanent: operator overloading (OD26), capability hiding (authority rule 5), derived equality, mutable global state (OD8), umbrella capabilities and aliases, old/quantifiers in contracts (OD117), lexical shadowing (OD67), and ghost code that affects execution. Ghost code itself is admitted as decided (OD81). Foreign function values reopen when typed extern fn types are admitted (OD4); concurrency reopens on R-0399's trigger.
legacy/docs/spec/SPEC.md:12580:- **P20** One home for binding decisions — Move the still-binding roadmap decisions (new compiler, retention contract, authority, allocation, Lean as the spec) into docs/decisions.md beside your language answers. The dated log becomes history; ROADMAP.md links to decisions.md and restates nothing.
